A settings save that is refused or times out no longer deletes or replaces
the stored Hugging Face / CivitAI token. PATCH /v1/config validates
credential values up front and writes the credential store last, only after
update_config has returned; before that the store is only read, so an error
response never follows a credential write. A credential write that fails
after the config save reports that the other settings were saved.

An unreadable model_source_credentials.json is reported as status_unknown in
the settings schema and "(status unknown)" in Settings. An unreadable
credential store or config.json is a 409 naming the file on the config,
media, tts and plugin-settings routes, and `localm config` reports it as an
ordinary error.

